# CD-DA audio: the .raw files are sox build artifacts, and the source tracks are
# both large and game data, so neither is kept in git.
#
# `tracklist` is ignored too, and is NOT hand-maintained: tools/extract_disc
# writes it alongside the tracks it extracts. It must still exist at build time
# -- shared.mk falls back to a bare `find` when it is absent, with no sort, so
# disc-track numbers would follow directory order and the wrong music would play
# with nothing in the build log to say so. Deleting it is safe only because
# data.bat regenerates it; deleting it and building without regenerating is not.
*.raw
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
tracklist
